invariant: INV-36
file: chapulin_tcp.zig
catches: test/zig-build-check.sh
reason: seal returns an empty side where ch_seal_in_place wrote a
  KeyUpdate record into side_buf, so a caller sends the records under the
  next key without the KeyUpdate that moves the peer to it, and the peer
  fails the first record with bad_record_mac. loop_key_update_run.zig,
  which requires the KeyUpdate an owed answer writes, and the SUITE=aesgcm
  loop's seal across the ceiling object (docs/decisions.md 248).

--- old
            return .{ .records = buf[0..result.records_len], .side = side_buf[0..result.side_len] };
--- new
            return .{ .records = buf[0..result.records_len], .side = side_buf[0..0] };
